    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0484" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>

                <head>118. Circular Telegram From the Secretary of State to All Diplomatic Missions
                    in the American Republics<anchor n="1" xml:id="d118-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-07-18T18:25:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18,
                                1956—6:25 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>37. President Eisenhower considering proposing in speech at Panama each American
                    President name personal and trusted representative to join in preparing concrete
                    recommendations for making OAS more effective instrument in those fields of
                    cooperative effort that affect the welfare of our peoples. Presidents could look
                    to these representatives for practical suggestions in economic, financial,
                    social and technical fields which OAS might usefully adopt.</p>
                <p>You may discuss this proposal in strict confidence with President your country to
                    ascertain whether he has any objection since President Eisenhower would like to
                    put proposal forward as idea viewed favorably by Presidents meeting Panama.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
